= The Security Council vote

Spain is competing with Turkey and New Zealand for two non-permanent seats on the UN Security Council for 2015–2016. The government's diplomats have lobbied for years; the vote in the General Assembly is days away. Rajoy asks the opposition to show a united front.

- @unsc_back: Back the bid publicly: this is Spain's seat, not the PP's
- @unsc_criticise: Back the bid, but criticise the government's aid cuts
- @unsc_silent: Say nothing

@unsc_back
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp += 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'un', 8); } !}
go-to: unsc_result

@unsc_criticise
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'un', 2); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'young', 1); } !}
go-to: unsc_result

@unsc_silent
go-to: unsc_result

@unsc_result
