= Portugal's "contraption"

In Lisbon, the socialist António Costa topples the centre-right minority government and governs with the support of the Communists, the Greens and the Left Bloc. The right calls it the *geringonça*, the contraption. It is exactly the kind of arrangement Spain's left is arguing about.

- @costa_model: Hail it as a model: the left can govern together
- @costa_cautious: Praise Costa, but say every country is different
- @costa_warning: Warn that Spain is not Portugal

@costa_model
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up += 6; Q.progressives_dissent -= 4; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'south', 6); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.5, 0); } !}

Costa calls to thank you. Susana Díaz's people note that you are already measuring the curtains for a government with Podemos.

@costa_cautious
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'south', 3); } !}

A diplomatic answer, and a door left ajar.

@costa_warning
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up -= 5; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; Q.progressives_dissent += 4; !}

The barons are reassured. Podemos quotes Lisbon at you for months.

