= Two per cent

At the NATO summit in Brussels, President Trump demands that every ally spend 2% of GDP on defence, and singles out the laggards. Spain spends 0.9%, among the lowest in the alliance.

- @nato_commit: Commit to a path towards 2%
- @nato_gradual: Promise gradual increases, with no date
- @nato_refuse: Refuse: Spain's priority is its welfare state

@nato_commit
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent += 8; Q.rel_up -= 8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'nato', 10); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'us', 8); window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); } if (Q.psoe_in_government) { Q.fiscal_adj += 0.2; } !}

Washington is pleased. Podemos calls it a militarist budget.

