= The pandemic

A new coronavirus is filling the hospitals of Madrid and Barcelona. On 14 March the government declares a state of alarm. Spain enters one of the strictest lockdowns in the world; tens of thousands will die; the economy will shrink by more than 10% this year. Party campaigns stop; the party saves money it cannot spend. [? if psoe_in_government = 1 : As Prime Minister, every decision is yours, and so is every death in the headlines. ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : The government asks for the opposition's votes to extend the state of alarm every two weeks. ?]

- @covid_strict: [? if psoe_in_government = 1 : A strict national lockdown, decided in Madrid ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : Support every extension of the state of alarm ?]
- @covid_regions: [? if psoe_in_government = 1 : Co-governance: the regions manage the measures ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : Support it, but demand the regions have a say ?]
- @covid_economy: [? if psoe_in_government = 1 : Protect the economy: lighter, shorter measures ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : Oppose the extensions: the government is improvising ?]

@covid_strict
on-arrival: {! if (Q.psoe_in_government) { Q.fiscal_adj += 0.5; Q.sanchez_authority += 6; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 2, homemakers: 1}); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {self_employed: 2, professionals: 0.5}); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 3); } } else { Q.rel_pp += 5; Q.sanchez_authority += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'pensioners', 1.5); } } !}

[? if psoe_in_government = 1 : The curve flattens. The furlough scheme (ERTE) protects millions of jobs. Shopkeepers and the self-employed are furious, and Vox drives through Madrid in caravans of honking cars. ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : Responsible opposition. The government thanks you; your critics say you have become the PP's crutch. ?]

@covid_regions
on-arrival: {! if (Q.psoe_in_government) { Q.fiscal_adj += 0.3; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 10; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 0.5}); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Madrid', 'pp', 1.04); } } else { Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 6; Q.rel_pp += 2; } !}

[? if psoe_in_government = 1 : The regions take charge, and seventeen different sets of rules confuse everyone. Madrid's president keeps her bars open and becomes a national figure. ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : The barons who govern regions are grateful. ?]

@covid_economy
