= The King Emeritus leaves

Under investigation in Switzerland and Spain over millions from Saudi Arabia, the former King Juan Carlos I leaves Spain for Abu Dhabi. Podemos demands a referendum on the monarchy.

- @monarchy_defend: Defend the institution: the King is not his father
- @monarchy_transparency: Demand transparency and an end to the King's legal immunity
- @monarchy_silence: Say as little as possible

@monarchy_defend
on-arrival: {! Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 5; Q.rel_up -= 8; Q.rel_pp += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'pensioners', 1.5); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -0.5); } !}

The PSOE as a party of State. Podemos calls you courtiers.

@monarchy_transparency
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 5; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 5; Q.rel_up += 5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'young', 1.5); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 0.8); } !}

The Royal Household is not pleased. Young voters are.

@monarchy_silence
on-arrival: institutionalists_dissent -= 1

The story runs for weeks without you.

@ayuso
title: Ayuso calls an election
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: ayuso_seen = 0 and madrid_pp = 1 and ((year = 2021 and month >= 3) or year >= 2022)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.ayuso_seen = 1;
if (Q.regions && Q.regions['Madrid']) { var y = Q.year, m = Q.month + 2; if (m > 12) { m -= 12; y += 1; } Q.regions['Madrid'].nextElection = y + '-' + (m < 10 ? '0' : '') + m + '-04'; Q.regions['Madrid'].lastWasSnap = true; }
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Madrid', 'pp', 1.15); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Madrid', 'cs', 0.6); }
!}

= Ayuso calls an election

In Murcia, Ciudadanos tries to topple the PP with the PSOE's help, and fails. In Madrid, Isabel Díaz Ayuso, fearing the same, dissolves her assembly first and calls an election under one word: *Libertad*. Pablo Iglesias leaves the national government to run against her.

- @madrid_all_in: Throw everything into Madrid
- @madrid_local: Let the Madrid socialists run their own campaign

@madrid_all_in
choose-if: funds >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough party funds (needs 2).
on-arrival: {! Q.funds -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Madrid', 'psoe', 1.04); } !}

You campaign in Madrid every weekend. If it goes badly, it will be your defeat as much as theirs.

@madrid_local
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 1; !}

A local campaign by a local candidate. The national stakes are obvious anyway.

@ceuta
title: Ceuta
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: ceuta_seen = 0 and ((year = 2021 and month >= 5) or year >= 2022)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.ceuta_seen = 1; Q.ceuta_severe = (Q.intl && Q.intl.maghreb < 45) ? 1 : 0; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {pensioners: 1 + Q.ceuta_severe, self_employed: 1 + Q.ceuta_severe, workers: 0.5 + Q.ceuta_severe}); } !}

= Ceuta

Angry that Spain admitted the Polisario leader Brahim Ghali to a Spanish hospital, Morocco's border guards step aside. [? if ceuta_severe = 1 : Ten thousand people, many of them children, swim and walk into Ceuta in two days. ?][? if ceuta_severe = 0 : Several thousand people cross into Ceuta before Rabat closes the border again. ?] Vox calls it an invasion.

- @ceuta_army: Send the army to the border and ask Brussels for support
- @ceuta_rabat: Calm things down with Rabat, quietly
- @ceuta_children: Protect the unaccompanied children first

@ceuta_army
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'maghreb', -8); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 5); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'pensioners', 1.5); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -0.8); } !}

Firm, and seen to be firm. Brussels declares Ceuta's border Europe's border.

@ceuta_rabat
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'maghreb', 6); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {pensioners: 0.5, self_employed: 0.5}); } !}

The crisis ends, the questions about what Spain conceded do not.

@ceuta_children
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'un', 4); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1); } !}

UNICEF praises Spain. Vox puts the children on its campaign posters.

@pardons
title: The pardons
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: pardons_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and cat_crisis_seen = 1 and cat_sentence_seen = 1 and ((year = 2021 and month >= 6) or year >= 2022)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: pardons_seen = 1

= The pardons

The independence leaders have served more than three years. ERC, on whose votes your government depends, asks for pardons. The Supreme Court advises against; the PP collects signatures in the street.

- @pardon_yes: Grant the pardons: "concord over revenge"
- @pardon_no: Refuse: the sentences stand

@pardon_yes
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 2; Q.rel_erc += 20; Q.rel_junts += 10; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 15; Q.rel_pp -= 10; Q.rel_cs -= 10; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {pp: 0.5, vox: 0.3, cs: 0.2}, {pensioners: 2, homemakers: 1.5, self_employed: 1.5}); window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'erc', 0.97); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.06); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1.5); } !}

The streets of Catalonia go quiet. The rest of Spain argues about it for a year.

@pardon_no
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_erc -= 20; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'pensioners', 1.5); } if (Q.depends_on_catalans) { Q.depends_on_catalans = 0; Q.lost_majority = 1; } !}

[? if lost_majority = 1 : ERC withdraws its support. Your government no longer has a majority. ?][? if lost_majority = 0 : The PP has nothing to campaign on. ERC has everything. ?]

@la_palma
title: The volcano
new-page: true
