= The Iberian exception

Electricity bills have tripled. Spain and Portugal ask Brussels to let them cap the price of gas used for electricity, arguing that the Iberian peninsula is an "energy island". [? if iberian_ok = 1 : With António Costa at your side and goodwill in Brussels, the Commission agrees. Bills fall within weeks. ?][? if iberian_ok = 0 : Without allies, the request stalls. Bills keep rising, and so does the anger. ?]

@nato_madrid
title: The Madrid summit
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: nato_madrid_seen = 0 and psoe_in_government = 1 and ((year = 2022 and month >= 6) or year >= 2023)
max-visits: 1
